cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "Cite the archived Zenodo release; the DOI resolves to the public record for this archive."
title: "Active Inference Language Model: A Fully Explicit Discrete Language System and a Gate-Audit Method"
abstract: >-
  AILM is a set of explicit discrete probabilistic language models implemented in
  pymdp, with named probabilities, preferences, habits and policy precision.
  Every quantitative claim resolves from
  a single-writer ledger, and every acceptance threshold is audited against a
  trivial baseline, a reference comparator and deliberately broken variants. The
  connected runtime executes a declared causal schedule of conditional updates;
  historical level and channel results retain their separate experimental scope.
type: software
